The important thing is that this reads as trajectory, not missing functionality.

4. Hard-code the three nodes now.
That is absolutely fine. You are not building an infrastructure benchmark. You are demonstrating a live process under deadline. The registry already gives you a path to later replace hard-coded seed data with an add-node workflow.

5. Make the deadline itself visible as a live state.
This is the one piece I think is worth adding now because it supports the uncertainty you are describing.

For example, in micro-type:

APPLICATION WINDOW / STILL OPEN

or

D0 · BEFORE SUBMISSION

Then after submission:

APPLICATION / SUBMITTED

and that state change can unlock the next stage.

That creates a very neat progression:

G_0 = \{*, /\}

then, before submission,

G_1 = \{+, *, /, \text{Ave}, \text{Mai}, \text{Kenn-Eerik}\}

then the jury scan gives an event,

G_1 \xrightarrow{\text{application activation}} E_1

and only after that do you unlock actual node addition.

So I would not spend the next hour building the dialog. It is not needed to make the application credible. The stronger move is to show an already populated but still clearly opening system.

